# 3D City Simulation with Three.js

A fully interactive 3D city simulation in the browser using Three.js. Features a grid-based city with procedural buildings, animated traffic lights, and AI-driven cars that obey traffic signals.

## Proposed Changes

### Project Structure

#### [NEW] index.html
Main entry point — loads Three.js from CDN, links CSS and JS files, contains the canvas mount and HUD overlay HTML.

#### [NEW] style.css
Glassmorphism-styled HUD panel, controls, stats display. Dark background, neon accent colors for a premium modern look.

#### [NEW] js/main.js
Scene bootstrap: renderer, camera, lighting (ambient + directional with shadows), fog, orbit controls. Animation loop.

#### [NEW] js/city.js
Procedural city generator:
- 6×6 grid of city blocks separated by roads
- Each block filled with 2–5 buildings (random height 10–60m, random muted colors)
- Ground plane with road texture pattern drawn via canvas
- Road markings (dashed center lines, crosswalks at intersections)
- Sidewalks along all roads

#### [NEW] js/traffic.js
Traffic light system:
- `TrafficLight` class: 3D pole + 3 light heads (red/yellow/green)
- State machine cycling: Green (N/S) → Yellow → Red → Green (E/W) → ...
- 4 traffic lights per intersection
- Exposes `getStateForDirection(dir)` → `"red" | "green" | "yellow"`

#### [NEW] js/vehicles.js
Vehicle system:
- `Car` class: detailed box-geometry car (body, roof, wheels, headlights, windows)
- Waypoint graph built from road grid — nodes at block centers and intersections
- `VehicleManager`: spawns cars at random entry points, assigns random routes
- Movement: cars accelerate/decelerate, check traffic light state before crossing intersections
- Lane-aware positioning (drive on right side of road)
- Cars slow down and stop behind other cars (simple following behavior)

#### [NEW] js/ui.js
HUD overlay logic:
- Live stats: car count, simulation time
- Slider: simulation speed (0.5× – 3×)
- Button: "Add Cars" (+5 cars)
- Button: "Day / Night" toggle (changes sky, adds emissive headlights at night)
- Minimap (optional 2D canvas top-down view)

---

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification (Browser)
1. Open `index.html` directly in Chrome/Edge (double-click or drag to browser)
2. Verify the 3D scene loads with a city grid visible
3. Use mouse to orbit (left-drag), pan (right-drag), zoom (scroll)
4. Confirm buildings of varied heights appear in city blocks
5. Confirm traffic lights cycle Red → Green → Yellow correctly at intersections
6. Confirm cars appear on roads and move
7. Confirm cars stop at red lights and proceed on green
8. Test "Add Cars" button — car count should increase
9. Test speed slider — animation should speed up/slow down
10. Test Day/Night toggle — sky should darken and headlights glow
